  "title": "Election Commission of India Faces Controversy Over SIR Revisions and Protests",
  "summary": "The Election Commission of India faced criticism over its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders following allegations of procedural issues, with Congress demanding immediate action to address concerns. The Commission defended its processes and claimed the changes to electoral rolls were upheld by legal standards.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Election Commission (EC) withdrew the SIR-related declaration from Form 6 in states where the electoral roll revision exercise concluded, citing the ECINET portal updates.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Delhi's Election Commission faced backlash over its handling of SIR orders, with a public audit revealing 100 voters misclassified as absent, shifted, or dead.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Congress accused the EC of breaching constitutional standards and demanded immediate action to address concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
